      <section class="hero wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">Declassified Archive · U.S. Army · 9 June 1983</div>
        <h1>THE GATEWAY PROCESS.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A full reader page for <em>Analysis and Assessment of Gateway Process</em>: the original document, its historical identity, the meaning of printed page 25, and a disciplined explanation of what “controlling the illusion” can—and cannot—mean.</p>
        <div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="#document">Read the Document</a><a class="btn alt" href="#page-25">Decode Page 25</a><a class="btn alt" href="https://www.cia.gov/readingroom/docs/CIA-RDP96-00788R001700210016-5.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Official Archive PDF ↗</a></div>
      </section>

      <section class="section wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">Document Identity</div>
        <h2>WHAT THIS FILE ACTUALLY IS.</h2>
        <p>The first page identifies the paper as a Department of the Army assessment prepared within the U.S. Army Operational Group at Fort George G. Meade. It is dated 9 June 1983 and signed by Lieutenant Colonel Wayne M. McDonnell. The document later entered the CIA Reading Room archive under record number <strong>CIA-RDP96-00788R001700210016-5</strong>.</p>
        <div class="source-grid">
          <div class="source-cell"><strong>Title</strong><span>Analysis and Assessment of Gateway Process</span></div>
          <div class="source-cell"><strong>Date</strong><span>9 June 1983</span></div>
          <div class="source-cell"><strong>Origin</strong><span>Department of the Army</span></div>
          <div class="source-cell"><strong>Author</strong><span>Wayne M. McDonnell, LTC</span></div>
          <div class="source-cell"><strong>Archive ID</strong><span>CIA-RDP96-00788R001700210016-5</span></div>
          <div class="source-cell"><strong>Evidence Rating</strong><span>Confirmed primary document</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary"><strong>Critical distinction:</strong> the file proves that an Army officer produced this assessment and that the government archived it. It does not, by itself, prove every neurological, cosmological, remote-viewing or out-of-body claim described inside it.</div>
      </section>

      <section id="document" class="section wrap page-jump">
        <div class="eyebrow">Primary Source Viewer</div>
        <h2>READ THE ORIGINAL 29-PAGE FILE.</h2>
        <div class="document-shell">
